  "body": "When a user's device is deleted - either manually, when they log out or when their account is deactivated - `to_device` messages aimed at that device are not deleted, and end up sitting in the database forever.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/a78016dadfb1680f5f77daae9948086b37cbeef8/synapse/handlers/device.py#L343-L417\r\n\r\nThere's no point in keeping them around, and should get rid of them when a device goes pop.\r\n\r\nRelated: https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/issues/3599",
